        "original_id": "1e4ee6c3-f30e-55b2-a723-781443cc32e2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Douglas SBD Dauntless\n- Ships: Japanese minesweeper Tama Maru No. 2, USS Lexington, USS Yorktown\n- Events: invasion of Lae-Salamaua, World War II\n- Places: Lae, New Guinea\n- Organizations: United States Navy, Douglas Aircraft\n\nFacts:\n- From 1940 through 1944, Douglas Aircraft manufactured the Douglas SBD Dauntless.\n- The Douglas SBD Dauntless was an American naval scout plane and dive bomber used during World War II.\n- On 10 March 1942, during the invasion of Lae-Salamaua, Japanese minesweeper Tama Maru No. 2 was damaged off Lae, New Guinea.\n- United States Navy Douglas SBD Dauntless dive bombers from the aircraft carriers USS Lexington and USS Yorktown damaged Tama Maru No. 2.",
